H(S) = #{admissible cells (e,s), s<=S},  S = 0..12: [1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 12, 16, 21, 26, 32, 38, 45, 53]

Does 36 (or any triangular / square number) occur more often than chance?
  pi_3(2^K): index where value = 36: [];
      triangular values (first 200 terms): [(0, 1), (3, 6), (8, 28), (22, 171), (27, 253), (163, 8515)]  [6 hits, ~6.5 expected by chance]
      square values: [(0, 1), (2, 4), (4, 9), (45, 676), (118, 4489), (191, 11664)]  [6 hits, ~4.6 expected by chance]
  pi_3(3^S): index where value = 36: [];
